  prose(<<~'CANONICAL_PROSE', origin: :published)
    ## Overview
    
    Sivruta~ is a Nightshelf void-mage of the Frozen Peace, bearer of two artifacts of considerable power, and a figure whose mythic standing derives not from ascent but from the deliberate act of going deeper when others rose. The canonical summary names them "lesser hero, sharper knife" against the backdrop of ☽'Otrolal the Watchful's more celebrated career. This is accurate as far as it goes. The deeper record suggests the distinction between lesser and sharper is not one Sivruta~ would contest.
    
    ## The Nisaemesius Campaign and Its Aftermath
    
    Sivruta~ emerged from the defense of ☽'slew Nisaemesius~ alongside Otrolal, the Nightshelf hero who wielded ☽'micseleia' Dagger and the shadow-craft of Hush☽ Twilight. Where Otrolal rose to open renown, Sivruta~ withdrew into the Berg's lower tunnels. Their name is spoken in the Glow-Fissure — a corruption breach-point of no small danger — with the kind of respect reserved for those who have traded something essential for competence. The nature of that trade is unrecorded. The cost is legible in the silence that surrounds them.
    
    During the Orca Incursion, Sivruta~'s void-blade scarred the raider Krathund Gnurl's left flank, leaving a dead patch where sensation never returned. Krathund Gnurl was later destroyed in the aftermath of the Wake-Singer blood-ritual known as the Grulkzul Omega Strike — a fact I note without editorial satisfaction.
    
    ## Artifacts
    
    **☽'visois' Mask.** A shadow-steel relic of the Great Thaw that chose its own wielders across generations. It hangs at Sivruta~'s throat on a chain of blackened fire-core links. The summary states the Mask chose them. The years since have been spent learning what that choice cost.
    
    **The Twilight-bells.** Retrieved from ☽'moth Silvesiris~ through corrupted tunnels, using the grimoire ☽'☽'numu' Witness as guide. Sivruta~ surrendered fire-cores as passage-tolls to The Cell — a territorial power in the deep tunnels — and encountered Otrolal's apparition in thin-veil territory. They refused to follow it into the deep. The passage opened. The bells cannot be owned, only carried; Sivruta~ accepted the burden. The two artifacts resonate with each other. What this resonance produces is not described in any source available to me.
    
    ## Current Activities
    
    Sivruta~ posts recruitment notices under the signature 'S~,' seeking applicants for retrieval work in passages where the pressure-sense reads wrong. Payment is offered in uncut fire-cores and a debt remembered. The notices do not mention what became of previous retrievers.
    
    Other Nightshelf leave extra rations at the memorial-stones when Sivruta~ passes. Not from pity. From the understanding that some debts are paid in silence.
  CANONICAL_PROSE
